## 7. Key Component Architecture

### 7.1 BeatGrid Component

This is the heart of the UI. It renders a grid where:
- **Rows** = instrument tracks (kick, snare, hi-hat, etc.)
- **Columns** = beat subdivisions (8 columns for 8th notes in 4/4, 16 for 16ths)
- **Cells** = individual steps that can be toggled on/off

```
┌──────────┬───┬───┬───┬───┬───┬───┬───┬───┐
│ Hi-Hat   │ ● │ ● │ ● │ ● │ ● │ ● │ ● │ ● │  (all 8th notes)
├──────────┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┤
│ Snare    │   │   │ ● │   │   │   │ ● │   │  (beats 2 & 4)
├──────────┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┤
│ Kick     │ ● │   │   │   │ ● │   │   │   │  (beats 1 & 3)
└──────────┴───┴───┴───┴───┴───┴───┴───┴───┘
                        ▲
                   Current beat
                   (highlighted column)
```

**Visual treatment:**
- Dark background (`bg-gray-900`)
- Active cells glow in instrument-specific colors (kick=red, snare=yellow, hihat=cyan, etc.)
- The current playback column gets a bright vertical highlight/pulse
- Beat 1 of each measure gets a slightly different column background to show measure boundaries
- Grid lines between columns use subtle `border-gray-700`

### 7.2 BpmControl Component

```
    ┌─────────────────────────────┐
    │         120 BPM             │  <- Large numeric display
    │   ─────────●────────────    │  <- Slider (40-240 range)
    │   [ - ]          [ + ]      │  <- Decrement/Increment by 1
    │       [ TAP TEMPO ]         │  <- Tap to set BPM
    └─────────────────────────────┘
```

**Tap Tempo algorithm:** Record the timestamps of the last 4 taps, compute average interval, convert to BPM. Discard if tap gap > 2 seconds (user paused).

### 7.3 Practice Mode Components

**Loop mode (default):** Pattern loops indefinitely. Simple.

**Tempo Ramp mode:**
```
    Start: [80] BPM    End: [140] BPM
    Increase by: [5] BPM every [4] bars

    Current: 95 BPM  |  Bars: 12/24  |  ████████░░░░
```

The scheduler checks bar count after each full loop. When `barsPerIncrement` bars have played, it increments BPM by `incrementBpm`, up to `endBpm`.

