## 7. Key Component Architecture

### 7.1 BeatGrid Component

This is the heart of the UI. It renders a grid where:
- **Rows** = instrument tracks (kick, snare, hi-hat, etc.)
- **Columns** = beat subdivisions (8 columns for 8th notes in 4/4, 16 for 16ths)
- **Cells** = individual steps that can be toggled on/off

```
┌──────────┬───┬───┬───┬───┬───┬───┬───┬───┐
│ Hi-Hat   │ ● │ ● │ ● │ ● │ ● │ ● │ ● │ ● │  (all 8th notes)
├──────────┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┤
│ Snare    │   │   │ ● │   │   │   │ ● │   │  (beats 2 & 4)
├──────────┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┼───┤
│ Kick     │ ● │   │   │   │ ● │   │   │   │  (beats 1 & 3)
└──────────┴───┴───┴───┴───┴───┴───┴───┴───┘
                        ▲
                   Current beat
                   (highlighted column)
```

**Visual treatment:**
- Dark background (`bg-gray-900`)
- Active cells glow in instrument-specific colors (kick=red, snare=yellow, hihat=cyan, etc.)
- The current playback column gets a bright vertical highlight/pulse
- Beat 1 of each measure gets a slightly different column background to show measure boundaries
- Grid lines between columns use subtle `border-gray-700`

